        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal and Compliance Framework for Nidhi Company</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Section 406, Companies Act 2013:</strong> Defines Nidhi as company working for cultivating thrift and savings among members. Central Government declares by notification. Source: <a href="https://www.mca.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mca.gov.in</a></p><p><strong>Nidhi Rules 2014:</strong> Governs formation, membership, deposits, lending, branches, compliance. Key: 7 members, 3 directors, Rs 10L capital, Rs 20L NOF, 200 members, NOF:deposit 1:20.</p><p><strong>Amendment Rules 2022:</strong> NDH-4 within 120 days. Fit-and-proper criteria. No 'Nidhi Limited' until declared. NDH-4 rejection blocks deposit acceptance.</p><p><strong>MCA Notification July 2024:</strong> Restricts 'Nidhi Limited' in company name unless Central Government declaration obtained.</p><p><strong>Prohibited Activities (Rule 6):</strong> No chit fund, hire purchase, leasing, insurance, securities, non-member deposits/loans, deposit advertising.</p><p><strong>Loan Restrictions (Rule 15):</strong> Only against gold/silver, immovable property, FD/RD, govt securities, LIC policies. Max rate: highest deposit rate + 7.5%.</p><p><strong>Penalties:</strong> Rs 5,000 for company and officers. Rs 500/day continuing default.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

