                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which office handles Nidhi company registration in Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Incorporation is filed with RoC Pune through MCA V3 portal using SPICE+. NDH-4 declaration filed with Central Government through MCA. Branch approvals outside district require Regional Director, Western Region (Mumbai) application. Patron's Pune office at Wagholi coordinates all filings.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can I register a Nidhi company online from Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Entire incorporation is online through MCA V3 portal. SPICE+, MOA, AOA, DSC, DIN all filed electronically. NDH-4 also filed online. No physical visit to RoC Pune required. Walk-in at Patron's Wagholi office for document verification and consultation.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the cost of Nidhi company registration in Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Professional fees start from Rs 25,000 covering SPICE+ filing, MOA/AOA, DSC, DIN, PAN/TAN, and RoC fees. NDH-4 support Rs 15,000-25,000 additional. Statutory minimum capital Rs 10 lakh. Rs 20 lakh NOF required before NDH-4. Total initial investment approximately Rs 20-25 lakh including capital.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does Nidhi company registration take in Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Incorporation at RoC Pune takes 10-15 working days. Then 120 days to achieve 200 members and Rs 20 lakh NOF for NDH-4. Central Government decides within 45 days of NDH-4 - if no decision, deemed approved. Total from start to Nidhi declaration: approximately 5-6 months.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can a Nidhi company accept deposits from the public?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. A Nidhi Company can accept deposits only from its members (shareholders). Cannot accept from general public, advertise for deposits, or pay brokerage for deposit mobilisation. Deposits accepted as FD, RD, and savings from members who have held equity shares for at least 6 months.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is RBI approval needed for a Nidhi company?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. Nidhi Companies are exempt from RBI core NBFC provisions because they deal exclusively with shareholder-members. No RBI licence, registration, or approval required. Regulated by MCA under Companies Act 2013 and Nidhi Rules 2014. This is the primary advantage over other finance structures.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What loans can a Nidhi company give?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Secured loans to members only against gold/silver ornaments, immovable property, fixed deposits and RD with the Nidhi, government securities, and LIC policies. Vehicle finance, micro-lending, unsecured loans, and loans to non-members are prohibited. Maximum interest rate: highest deposit rate + 7.5%.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is NDH-4 and when must it be filed?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>NDH-4 is the application filed with Central Government for declaring the company as Nidhi under Section 406. Must be filed within 120 days of incorporation with 200 members, Rs 20 lakh NOF, and fit-and-proper declarations. If no decision from MCA within 45 days, deemed approved.</p></div>
